  <h2>2. AI Automation Risk Landscape</h2>
  <p>Automation risk is not distributed evenly. This section examines how AI risk scores vary across job titles, countries, experience levels, and time—revealing where the greatest vulnerabilities lie.</p>

  <h3>2.1 Risk by Job Title</h3>
  <p>The data reveals a stark hierarchy of automation vulnerability. Business Analysts and Data Analysts occupy the highest-risk tier, with scores above 0.65. Software Engineers and Product Managers sit in a middle tier (0.40–0.45). Technical specialists—AI Researchers, ML Engineers, Cybersecurity Analysts, Cloud Engineers, and DevOps Engineers—form the lowest-risk cluster, all scoring below 0.36.</p>

  <table>
